ree="Destruction",name="Aftermath",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Shadowburn",r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r=3,max=3},{tree="Destruction",name="Conflagrate",r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[547],r=1,max=1},{tree="Destruction",name=S[573],r=3,max=3},{tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r=5,max=5},{tree="Destruction",name="Incinerate",r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Destruction",name="Bane",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=19,tree="Destruction",name=S[369],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=20,l2=20,tree="Destruction",name="Shadowburn",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=25,tree="Destruction",name="Ruin",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=26,l2=28,tree="Destruction",name=S[417],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=29,tree="Destruction",name="Conflagrate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="Destruction",name=S[547],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=33,tree="Destruction",name=S[573],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=34,l2=38,tree="Destruction",name="Aftermath",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=39,l2=39,tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r1=1,r2=1,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Destruction",name="Incinerate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=44,tree="Destruction",name=S[496],r1=2,r2=5,max=5},{l1=45,l2=49,tree="Affliction",name="Suppression",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=50,l2=54,tree="Demonology",name=S[433],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=55,l2=56,tree="Demonology",name=S[477],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=57,l2=59,tree="Demonology",name=S[385],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=60,l2=60,tree="Demonology",name=S[286],r1=1,r2=1,max=1}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[386]},{t="p",s="legend",x="|cff71d5ffBlue text was updated for the WoW Forever hotfixes up to 10 November and is awaiting final review.|r"},{t="h1",x="Destruction",sub=S[443]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Hard-hitting Fire spells with two instant finishers: keep Immolate up, weave Shadowburn and Conflagrate to power Shadow and Flame, fill with Incinerate, and let Ruin turn critical strikes into big hits."},{t="pills",list={S[392],S[423]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[546]},{t="h2",x=S[329]},{t="p",x="Destruction feels good from the first points: faster casts, cheaper spells and harder critical hits. The leveling point order below follows the same path the build’s core takes at level 30."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Faster casts, cheaper spells"},{t="p",x="Bane (10–14) shortens Shadow Bolt and Immolate, and Improved Shadow Bolt (15–19) strengthens your early filler. Send your demon in, Immolate, then Shadow Bolt; finish low enemies with your wand to save mana."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Big crits and two finishers"},{t="p",x="Shadowburn at 20 and Ruin from 21 make critical strikes hit far harder. Agonizing Flames boosts every Destruction spell, Conflagrate adds a second instant, and Bane of Havoc at 30 lets you cleave two tough enemies. Fire and Brimstone (31–33) raises Conflagrate’s critical chance, and Aftermath (34–38) adds 50% to Immolate’s initial damage."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Incinerate and Shadow and Flame"},{t="p",x="Incinerate arrives at 40 and hits harder on Immolated targets. Shadow and Flame keeps Immolate alive through Conflagrate and refunds Shadowburn’s Soul Shard, so both finishers go on cooldown. Shadowburn also raises your Fire damage by 20% for 20 seconds, which this build plays around. Suppression 5/5 by 49 adds hit, then 11 Demonology points add Stamina, armor and Demonic Sacrifice at 60: sacrifice the Succubus for 15% more Fire damage."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[367]},{t="h2",x=S[392]},{t="p",x=S[47]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[394]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[351]},{t="p",x=S[70]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="This build plays around Fire damage: keep Immolate up, use Shadowburn to keep Shadow and Flame’s 20% Fire bonus active, Conflagrate on cooldown without losing Immolate, and fill with Incinerate on Immolated targets. Sacrifice the Succubus for another 15% Fire damage once Demonic Sacrifice is trained."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[457]},{t="h2",x=S[375]},{t="p",x="Destruction wants hit until the cap, then spell power, haste and critical strike for its direct casts. Ruin and Improved Searing Pain make crits hit very hard."},{t="h3",x=S[528]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[571],x="Fire damage counts for most of your spells"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=S[323]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spirit",x="faster recovery"},{t="p",s="small",x="Fire damage is worth about two thirds of plain spell damage to this build; Shadow damage about a third."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spell power",x="Fire damage counts too"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Haste",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[503],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Crit and hit are close in value. With five points in Suppression you need 12% hit from gear."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[48]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[376]},{t="h2",x=S[409]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. While leveling, omit talents and spells you have not learned."},{t="h4",x="Open with your demon and Curse"},{t="p",x="Send your demon in, apply your Curse (Curse of the Elements for dungeon bosses), and pre-cast a Shadow Bolt so it lands together with your Immolate."},{t="h4",x="Keep Immolate up"},{t="p",x="Immolate is the only effect you must maintain. Aftermath raises its initial hit, Conflagrate needs it, and Incinerate deals 25% more to an Immolated target. With 5/5 Shadow and Flame, Conflagrate no longer consumes Immolate."},{t="h4",x="Use both finishers on cooldown"},{t="p",x="Conflagrate grants 20% Shadow damage and Shadowburn grants 20% Fire damage for 20 seconds through Shadow and Flame, and Shadowburn refunds its Soul Shard instantly. Fire and Brimstone gives Conflagrate extra critical chance, which Ruin turns into very large hits."},{t="h4",x="Choose the filler for your gear"},{t="p",x="Incinerate is your main filler on an Immolated target: with Shadowburn’s Fire bonus and the Succubus sacrifice, your Fire spells hit hardest. Use Shadow Bolt only while Conflagrate’s Shadow bonus is up and your Shadow damage is higher. Exact level-60 priorities still need testing."},{t="h4",x="Cleave with Bane of Havoc"},{t="p",x="On two tough enemies, put Bane of Havoc on the one you are not attacking; 15% of your damage to other targets also hits it. Havoc is a Bane, so it cannot share a target with your Bane of Agony|cff71d5ff, and it triggers the global cooldown, so apply it between casts|r. Rain of Fire and Hellfire feed it in packs, but let the tank establish threat first."},{t="h4",x="Manage mana and Soul Shards"},{t="p",x="Destruction burns mana quickly. Improved Life Tap and Spirit improve every tap; Drain Life gets the health back. Use Drain Soul on dying enemies whenever you need more Soul Shards."},{t="abil",names={"Shadow Bolt","Immolate","Conflagrate","Shadowburn","Incinerate",S[547],S[424],"Rain of Fire"}},{t="h3",x=S[482]},{t="p",x="This build uses both schools. General spell power is the safest upgrade; Fire damage strengthens Immolate, Incinerate and Conflagrate, Shadow damage strengthens Shadow Bolt and Shadowburn. Ruin doubles the value of critical strikes, so Intellect and critical chance climb in value with gear. 5/5 Suppression already gives 5% hit; haste on gear speeds up your hard casts."},{t="p",x=S[54]},{t="h3",x=S[319]},{t="p",x="Shadowburn refunds its own Soul Shard with Shadow and Flame, but keep spares for summons, Healthstones and a Soulstone. Use Create Firestone (Fire damage and critical chance) or Create Spellstone (Shadow damage and haste) to match the school your gear favors."},{t="p",x="Without Demonology points, the Succubus is the strongest damage demon and the Imp brings Blood Pact Stamina for the group. Use the Felhunter for Spell Lock in caster-heavy dungeons. Bring Curse of the Elements unless another Warlock already covers it."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[444]},{t="h2",x=S[304]},{t="p",x=S[46]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[38]},{t="macro",n=S[395],x=S[62],code=S[141]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[124],code=S[154]},{t="macro",n=S[334],x=S[65],code=S[113]},{t="macro",n=S[373],x=S[77],code=S[132]},{t="macro",n=S[529],x=S[97],code=S[181]},{t="macro",n=S[495],x=S[114],code=S[172]},{t="macro",n=S[377],x=S[112],code=S[120]},{t="macro",n=S[445],x=S[106],code=S[157]},{t="macro",n=S[435],x=S[100],code=S[155]},{t="macro",n=S[368],x=S[101],code=S[189]},{t="macro",n=S[504],x=S[144],code=S[246]},{t="macro",n=S[410],x=S[102],code=S[216]},{t="macro",n=S[572],x=S[201],code=S[335]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Bane of Havoc",x="Place Havoc on the second enemy under your pointer without leaving your main target. It cannot share a target with your Bane of Agony.",code="#showtooltip Bane of Havoc\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Bane of Havoc"},{t="macro",n="Conflagrate / Shift Immolate",x="Normal press casts Conflagrate. Hold Shift to Immolate first; the macro does not check whether Immolate is already on the target.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Immolate; [harm,nodead] Conflagrate"},{t="macro",n="Shadowburn finisher",x="Keep your instant Shadow finisher on its own key. With Shadow and Flame its Soul Shard is refunded, so it can be used on cooldown.",code="#showtooltip Shadowburn\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Shadowburn"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[195]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[505]},{t="h2",x=S[352]},{t="p",x=S[51]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[36]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[378]},{t="h2",x=S[349]},{t="p",x=S[53]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[396]},{t="h2",x=S[330]},{t="p",x=S[28]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[379]},{t="h2",x=S[301]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[364]},{t="kicker",x=S[506]},{